think Chose contract asserts: the SLC definition of done asks two asserts per new or touched function. No prior lap measured whether mantra and tally functions meet it.
think Measured with a brace-depth walk over tracked mantra and tally Rye files, run once and kept in /tmp, not in the tree. It counts assert call tokens per function body.
think Result: 772 functions, 321 with zero asserts, 459 with fewer than two. After excluding witness, self-test, demo, and runner names, 188 production-like functions have zero asserts.
think Ruled: the governing rule is a ratchet on touch, not a red. An untouched function owes no asserts and books no REDS row, so this lap opens no claim and makes no code edit.
